| **Demand Destruction** | High | High memory costs are being passed to consumers (Apple/Microsoft), risking a demand ceiling and price-sensitive pullbacks. |
| **Supply Glut Risk** | Medium | News indicates significant new capacity is coming online; historical "boom-and-bust" cycles suggest a looming price collapse. |
| **Concentration Risk** | High | Revenue is heavily dependent on a small group of hyperscalers; any capex cooling (e.g., Microsoft's recent performance) creates a single-point failure. |

